From: <your name and email>
Date: 2026-08-24
Subject: [PATCH] Add an Xtensa constant-time assembly path

mbedtls_ct_bool(), mbedtls_ct_if() and mbedtls_ct_uint_lt() have hand-written
assembly for Arm, AArch64, x86-64 and x86. Every other architecture uses the
generic C implementations, which are built out of mbedtls_ct_compiler_opaque()
barriers - six of them for a single
mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(a, b), 1, 0).

On Xtensa (ESP32) that costs about 44 CPU cycles where mbedTLS 3.6 used a
single compare, because on top of the barriers GCC declines to inline the
result at -Os, so each use becomes an out-of-line call with a register-window
entry and stack spills. Since mbedtls_mpi_core_sub() and
mbedtls_mpi_core_mla() were made constant time (mbedtls 4b4869a15 and
TF-PSA-Crypto 77bd4798), that lands directly on the bignum hot path: an n x n
mbedtls_mpi_core_mul() runs the changed mla line exactly n times, and each
mbedtls_mpi_core_montmul() performs 6n such operations.

Measured on an ESP32-D0WD-V3 at 240 MHz (Xtensa LX6, GCC 14.2, -Os), against
mbedTLS 3.6.6 built from ESP-IDF v5.5.5, offline, RSA/MPI accelerator off:

    ecdsa_verify P-256   3.6.6 245.12 ms   4.1.0 327.75 ms  (+33.7%)
    ecp_mul     P-256    3.6.6 113.92 ms   4.1.0 151.56 ms  (+33.0%)
    mpi_inv_mod P-256    3.6.6   8.66 ms   4.1.0  12.23 ms  (+41.2%)
    mpi_mul     256-bit  3.6.6   9.78 us   4.1.0  11.28 us  (+15.4%)

With this patch 4.1.0 returns to parity or better:

    ecdsa_verify P-256   243.19 ms  (-0.8% vs 3.6.6)
    ecp_mul     P-256    113.99 ms  (+0.1%)
    mpi_inv_mod P-256      7.59 ms  (-12.3%)
    mpi_mul     256-bit    9.80 us  (+0.2%)

The patch has three parts:

1. Xtensa assembly for the three primitives, mirroring the existing Arm
   sequences. Xtensa has no and-not, so ~x is built with movi -1 / xor.
   Verified branch-free: mbedtls_mpi_core_sub() disassembles to a single
   conditional branch, the loop back-edge on the public limb count - the same
   as the stock build, where a plain-C implementation has three.

2. always_inline on the three primitives. Assembly already makes them opaque
   to the optimiser, but at -Os GCC still leaves them out of line, and on
   Xtensa each call costs a register-window entry plus spills. With it,
   mbedtls_mpi_core_sub() contains no calls at all.

3. mbedtls_mpi_core_sub() and mbedtls_mpi_core_mla() use
   mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if_else_0(cond, 1) instead of
   mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if(cond, 1, 0). The former is (condition & if1); the
   latter has to build ~condition through a barrier. Architecture-independent,
   and separately verified constant-flow clean.

A C-level fix was tried first and rejected. Rewriting the generic
mbedtls_ct_uint_lt() as the branchless six-operation sequence in plain C is
faster, but clang 22 -O2 recognises the idiom, re-derives "x < y" and emits a
conditional branch; MemSan constant-flow testing catches it. Keeping barriers
on the two inputs is not enough either - the barriers hide values, not
structure. That is presumably why the assembly paths exist, and Xtensa simply
never got one.

Constant-flow testing was done with MBEDTLS_TEST_CONSTANT_FLOW_MEMSAN, clang,
CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=MemSanDbg, MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM unset so the generic C path is
the one under test, against TF-PSA-Crypto main. Note that
test_suite_bignum_core's own mpi_core_sub / mpi_core_mla cases cannot be used
in that configuration: they compare the returned carry while the inputs are
still marked secret, and the carry is secret-derived, so they report for any
implementation - including unmodified upstream. On x86 builds with
MBEDTLS_HAVE_ASM the inline assembly launders the MemSan poison and they pass,
which means the generic C path is currently not covered by constant-flow
testing at all. A harness that unpoisons outputs before touching them
distinguishes correctly: unmodified upstream passes, a plain-C carry fails.
The Xtensa assembly cannot be MemSan-tested (no MemSan for Xtensa); it rests
on the same argument as the existing Arm and x86 paths, plus the disassembly
check above.

---
diff --git a/drivers/builtin/src/bignum_core.c b/drivers/builtin/src/bignum_core.c
index fc1b537..43b29e0 100644
--- a/drivers/builtin/src/bignum_core.c
+++ b/drivers/builtin/src/bignum_core.c
@@ -452,10 +452,10 @@ mbedtls_mpi_uint mbedtls_mpi_core_sub(mbedtls_mpi_uint *X,
     mbedtls_mpi_uint c = 0;
 
     for (size_t i = 0; i < limbs; i++) {
-        mbedtls_mpi_uint z = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(A[i], c),
-                                                    1, 0);
+        mbedtls_mpi_uint z = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if_else_0(
+            mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(A[i], c), 1);
         mbedtls_mpi_uint t = A[i] - c;
-        c = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(t, B[i]), 1, 0) + z;
+        c = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if_else_0(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(t, B[i]), 1) + z;
         X[i] = t - B[i];
     }
 
@@ -493,7 +493,7 @@ mbedtls_mpi_uint mbedtls_mpi_core_mla(mbedtls_mpi_uint *d, size_t d_len,
 
     while (excess_len--) {
         *d += c;
-        c = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(*d, c), 1, 0);
+        c = mbedtls_ct_mpi_uint_if_else_0(mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(*d, c), 1);
         d++;
     }
 
diff --git a/utilities/constant_time_impl.h b/utilities/constant_time_impl.h
index 334764e..79c58e6 100644
--- a/utilities/constant_time_impl.h
+++ b/utilities/constant_time_impl.h
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@
 #define MBEDTLS_CT_X86_64_ASM
 #elif defined(__i386__)
 #define MBEDTLS_CT_X86_ASM
+#elif defined(__XTENSA__)
+#define MBEDTLS_CT_XTENSA_ASM
 #endif
 #endif
 
@@ -113,6 +115,7 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_uint_t mbedtls_ct_compiler_opaque(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x)
 #endif
 
 /* Convert a number into a condition in constant time. */
+__attribute__((always_inline))
 static inline mbedtls_ct_condition_t mbedtls_ct_bool(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x)
 {
     /*
@@ -176,6 +179,18 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_condition_t mbedtls_ct_bool(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x)
                   :
                   );
     return (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) x;
+#elif defined(MBEDTLS_CT_XTENSA_ASM) && defined(MBEDTLS_CT_SIZE_32)
+    uint32_t s;
+    asm volatile ("neg   %[s], %[x]                               \n\t"
+                  "or    %[x], %[s], %[x]                         \n\t"
+                  "srai  %[x], %[x], 31                           \n\t"
+                  :
+                  [s] "=&a" (s),
+                  [x] "+&a" (x)
+                  :
+                  :
+                  );
+    return (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) x;
 #else
     const mbedtls_ct_uint_t xo = mbedtls_ct_compiler_opaque(x);
 #if defined(_MSC_VER)
@@ -198,6 +213,7 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_condition_t mbedtls_ct_bool(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x)
 #endif
 }
 
+__attribute__((always_inline))
 static inline mbedtls_ct_uint_t mbedtls_ct_if(mbedtls_ct_condition_t condition,
                                               mbedtls_ct_uint_t if1,
                                               mbedtls_ct_uint_t if0)
@@ -257,6 +273,24 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_uint_t mbedtls_ct_if(mbedtls_ct_condition_t condition,
                   :
                   );
     return if1;
+#elif defined(MBEDTLS_CT_XTENSA_ASM) && defined(MBEDTLS_CT_SIZE_32)
+    /* Xtensa has no and-not, so ~condition is built with movi -1 / xor. */
+    uint32_t n, t;
+    asm volatile ("movi  %[n], -1                                 \n\t"
+                  "xor   %[n], %[condition], %[n]                 \n\t"
+                  "and   %[t], %[condition], %[if1]               \n\t"
+                  "and   %[n], %[n], %[if0]                       \n\t"
+                  "or    %[t], %[t], %[n]                         \n\t"
+                  :
+                  [n] "=&a" (n),
+                  [t] "=&a" (t)
+                  :
+                  [condition] "a" (condition),
+                  [if1] "a" (if1),
+                  [if0] "a" (if0)
+                  :
+                  );
+    return (mbedtls_ct_uint_t) t;
 #else
     mbedtls_ct_condition_t not_cond =
         (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) (~mbedtls_ct_compiler_opaque(condition));
@@ -264,6 +298,7 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_uint_t mbedtls_ct_if(mbedtls_ct_condition_t condition,
 #endif
 }
 
+__attribute__((always_inline))
 static inline mbedtls_ct_condition_t mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x, mbedtls_ct_uint_t y)
 {
 #if defined(MBEDTLS_CT_AARCH64_ASM) && (defined(MBEDTLS_CT_SIZE_32) || defined(MBEDTLS_CT_SIZE_64))
@@ -343,6 +378,26 @@ static inline mbedtls_ct_condition_t mbedtls_ct_uint_lt(mbedtls_ct_uint_t x, mbe
                   :
                   );
     return (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) x;
+#elif defined(MBEDTLS_CT_XTENSA_ASM) && defined(MBEDTLS_CT_SIZE_32)
+    uint32_t s, n, t;
+    asm volatile ("xor   %[s], %[x], %[y]                         \n\t"
+                  "sub   %[t], %[x], %[y]                         \n\t"
+                  "movi  %[n], -1                                 \n\t"
+                  "xor   %[n], %[s], %[n]                         \n\t"
+                  "and   %[t], %[t], %[n]                         \n\t"
+                  "and   %[s], %[s], %[y]                         \n\t"
+                  "or    %[t], %[t], %[s]                         \n\t"
+                  "srai  %[t], %[t], 31                           \n\t"
+                  :
+                  [s] "=&a" (s),
+                  [n] "=&a" (n),
+                  [t] "=&a" (t)
+                  :
+                  [x] "a" (x),
+                  [y] "a" (y)
+                  :
+                  );
+    return (mbedtls_ct_condition_t) t;
 #else
     /* Ensure that the compiler cannot optimise the following operations over x and y,
      * even if it knows the value of x and y.
